# Nougat Extraction — PENDING

**Status:** PENDING central Nougat parse

**Paper:** Belovs (2012), arXiv:1205.1534
**Title:** Learning-Graph-Based Quantum Algorithm for k-distinctness
**Author:** Aleksandrs Belovs (University of Latvia)

**Fallback:** The full paper text was extracted with `pdftotext -layout` (part
of Xpdf/Poppler) and is available at `../work/paper.txt`. Belovs's paper is a
LaTeX preprint with heavy math notation (adversary bound matrices, learning-
graph flows, weight assignments); Nougat's math-aware OCR would give a cleaner
markdown+LaTeX rendering than the plain pdftotext dump used for the numerical
replication.  Nougat is not installed in this environment (no CUDA-capable
node available under this sub-agent's compute quota, and Marker/Nougat are
GPU-heavy for math-heavy quantum-computing papers).

The replication in `../report/evidence/belovs_kdist.py` implements the paper's
Eq. (12) directly from the equations transcribed in `../report/REPORT.tex`;
no downstream tool consumes this extraction file for the numerical result.

To regenerate:

```bash
pip install nougat-ocr
nougat ../paper.pdf -o ../extraction/  # writes 1205.1534.mmd
mv ../extraction/1205.1534.mmd ../extraction/nougat.mmd
```
